cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this working governance method and include the exact Git commit used. No release or DOI is assigned to this remediation."
title: "AI Assistance Governance: A Working Method/Profile for Bounded AI Participation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Banasihan
    given-names: Mark Julius
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-8121-2878"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mj3b/rgds-ai-governance"
url: "https://github.com/mj3b/rgds-ai-governance"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Working governance method/profile for bounded AI participation in consequential
  decisions, with a two-part AI Dependency Test separating structural record
  completeness from substantive independence. RGDS records assigned human
  ownership and approval; practical influence requires separate assessment.
  Framework crosswalks are interpretive and do not establish compliance,
  conformity, certification, or regulator acceptance. No field effectiveness
  or independent validation is claimed.
keywords:
  - AI assistance governance
  - decision evidence
  - human authority
